      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "HTTP::Session2 versions before 1.12 for Perl for Perl may generate weak session ids using the rand() function.  The HTTP::Session2 session id generator returns a SHA-1 hash seeded with the built-in rand function, the epoch time, and the PID. The PID will come from a small set of numbers, and the epoch time may be guessed, if it is not leaked from the HTTP Date header. The built-in rand() function is unsuitable for cryptographic usage.  HTTP::Session2 after version 1.02 will attempt to use the /dev/urandom device to generate a session id, but if the device is unavailable (for example, under Windows), then it will revert to the insecure method described above.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
